Z||000005||batboy||02-19-2000||11:00 PM||||I found this info on Ed Park's webpage:<P>SUNROOF NOISES<P>Rattle would be from hinges plastic coating rubbed off. Popping/creaking is in all likely hood roof panel nuts loose. <P>Hinges are still available for about $6.50 ea, but some people have used heat shrink to coat theirs. Nuts require removing headliner to access.<P>SUNROOF PROBLEMS<P>Q: Anyone know where I can find the rubber grommets for a sunroof ? The ones that are on mine are about shot, and I believe that it is time to replace them. The clips that hold the window are so loose, I am afraid the sunroof may come off while I am driving. Could be a bummer, I imagine the sunroofs are quite expensive.<P>A: They are available from Pontiac, and now are a nut with a soft seal built in, as there are no nut gaskets available. These will correct 99% of all sunroof leaks, but if the latch is not quite tight, then order the spacer that goes under the latch.||||reg||1
